1. **The A11 mapping is incomplete.** Amendment §A gives CONFIG expressions for CP1 and CP3 and a decay-end expression for CP4. CP2 specifies a fixed source twin and explains the envelope value there. CP2b, CP3b, and CP5 give conditions that hold at their twins without showing how the harness derives those evaluation instants from CONFIG. CP4 also requires a shrink assertion for both `or` and `softer`, while the final log only shows `softer` at 8500 ms. I reproduced the recorded values and the CP3 timing swap from 7500 to 5600 ms using the on-disk evaluator. To clear A11, file the executable mapping that derives the source-twin instants from CONFIG and preserves the amended source anchors, then record the rerun with both CP4 shrink words and the CP3 timing swap. [Plan amendment §A](/home/hatch/workspace/goals/diy-building-and-real-learning/hidden_files/study/recreations/T197-volume-ramp/plan-amendment-cycle035.md:18) · [Build record, final harness](/home/hatch/workspace/goals/diy-building-and-real-learning/hidden_files/study/recreations/T197-volume-ramp/build-record.md:46)
2. **The fit result covers a different playback size.** The zero-HIT fit table models a 360×640 stage. The comparison iframe is 360×203, and the renderer scales type from stage height. At the comparison height, the fit table’s own model gives `203 × 0.061 × 0.45 × 0.72 ≈ 4.0 px` of shrink-state ink height against its approximately 11 px floor. The visible FIT-FAIL check uses a stage percentage, so the same shrink state clears that check at either height. The fit record needs a comparison-size result and a matching playback configuration before its zero-HIT claim can cover that surface. [Fit table](/home/hatch/workspace/goals/diy-building-and-real-learning/hidden_files/study/recreations/T197-volume-ramp/fit-table.md:3) · [Comparison dimensions](/home/hatch/workspace/goals/diy-building-and-real-learning/hidden_files/study/recreations/T197-volume-ramp/comparison.html:4) · [Renderer](/home/hatch/workspace/goals/diy-building-and-real-learning/hidden_files/study/recreations/T197-volume-ramp/recreation.html:206)
3. **The build is CONFIG-driven and generated.** The renderer builds spans from CONFIG, resolves one shared shrink envelope, and applies CONFIG values to timing, typography, and guide geometry. Both scripts parsed, the filed hashes matched, and the recreation asset scan returned zero hits. The census does incorrectly say the CSS `line-height:1.25` was removed. It remains in the stylesheet and receives an inline CONFIG override. [CONFIG census](/home/hatch/workspace/goals/diy-building-and-real-learning/hidden_files/study/recreations/T197-volume-ramp/config-census.md:31) · [Recreation source](/home/hatch/workspace/goals/diy-building-and-real-learning/hidden_files/study/recreations/T197-volume-ramp/recreation.html:178)
4. **The fidelity plan names its departures.** It accounts for the transient `louder` peak, persistent shared shrink, omitted section furniture and ornament, and unmeasured easing. It also records that the build is already marking `louder` spoken at the 55.0 s twin where the source observation reports it white. CP2b’s recorded PASS covers size and weight only. Rendered continuous weight remains explicitly unverified. [Build record, construction and fidelity](/home/hatch/workspace/goals/diy-building-and-real-learning/hidden_files/study/recreations/T197-volume-ramp/build-record.md:12) · [Source observation and weight limitation](/home/hatch/workspace/goals/diy-building-and-real-learning/hidden_files/study/recreations/T197-volume-ramp/build-record.md:23)

